``fset`` and ``fdel`` of a property defined with the ``@property`` decorator are
now inferred as ``None`` when the class body has no ``@name.setter`` or
``@name.deleter``, matching the runtime, and ``fdel`` of a property that has a
deleter is inferred as that function. Previously ``fset`` raised
``InferenceError`` (which crashed pylint on ``C.p.fset``) and ``fdel`` was not
known at all. The accessors of a property built by calling ``property()`` stay
uninferable.

Closes pylint-dev/pylint#8739
